\f0\b \cf2 Color Palette Concept (in the MonotriWorkFrame)\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 The color palette is NOT a continuous range of colors. Instead, a collection of colors is systematically arranged by hue. There are 36 hues that cover the full range, and in each hue the color samples are arranged the same way, as a system. The system consists of \'93equal-white\'94 series and \'93equal-black\'94 series which form the two diagonals. These series contain colors that are related by containing the same amount of either white or black, and then vertically there are the \'93shadow series\'94 which also contain related colors. For each hue there is a \'93monochrome triangle\'94 that has the pure Hue at one corner (such as a pure Red hue, or a pure Blue hue), with pure Black at the bottom corner, and pure White at the top corner. This systematic arrangement provides a quick way to apply predefined colors, referred to as \'93positions\'94 in the system:\
\
\'97 Selection is always fundamentally by shape, not by color. The meaning of this will become clear with use of the app.\
\'97 The \'93palette\'94 is the current collection of colors for all the shapes in the Template.\
\'97 The colors of the \'93palette\'94 are in different \'93positions\'94 in the monochrome triangles.\
\'97 The \'93status icon\'94 is the type of visual square that surrounds some positions in the monochrome triangle. The status icon is a form of high-lighting.\
\'97 Read this twice: The current status of all color positions always relates to the shapes in the Template. Every shape has a color, and each color is in some \'93position\'94.\
\'97 Icons clarify selected positions, versus \'93occupied\'94 positions. Selected shapes have selected positions. \
\'97 An \'93occupied\'94 position is a color that is in use, but it may not be currently selected (this means that no shape with that color is currently selected).\
\'97 Every selected position is an \'93occupied\'94 position. See the full explanation of this in the last paragraph below.\
\'97 All \'93occupied\'94 positions and selected positions are shown with status icons, even if they are NOT in the hue currently being displayed.\
\'97 The status icon is different if the color is in the hue currently being displayed. See the full explanation of this in the last paragraph below.\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

